---
/**
 * API index at /api/.
 *
 * The JSON endpoints themselves are static mirrors written into public/api/
 * by scripts/fetch-content.mjs, so they ship with the build and need no
 * server. This page is the documentation for them, which the old llms.txt
 * advertised before it existed: Search Console reported /api/ as a 404
 * because we pointed crawlers at an index we had never built.
 *
 * The endpoint list is declared here rather than read from disk because the
 * descriptions are editorial. If fetch-content.mjs gains an endpoint, add it
 * here too; the shape check below at least keeps the page honest about the
 * ones it claims.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';

const endpoints = [
  { file: 'laws.json', name: 'AI laws by state', page: '/ai-laws/',
    desc: 'Per-jurisdiction bill counts and the index behind every state page, for all 50 states, DC, Puerto Rico, and Congress.' },
  { file: 'glossary.json', name: 'AI glossary', page: '/ai-glossary/',
    desc: 'Every tracked AI term with its plain-English definition, origin, example, and category.' },
  { file: 'lawsuits.json', name: 'AI lawsuit tracker', page: '/ai-lawsuits/',
    desc: 'Every tracked case with parties, court, claims, status, docket timeline, and the CourtListener record.' },
  { file: 'compliance.json', name: 'Compliance frameworks', page: '/ai-compliance/',
    desc: 'The framework index: scope, obligations, and deadlines for each regime we track.' },
  { file: 'tools.json', name: 'AI tools directory', page: '/ai-tools/',
    desc: 'Tool catalog with categories and the researched profiles behind the directory pages.' },
  { file: 'companies.json', name: 'AI companies', page: '/companies/',
    desc: 'Company index keyed by the stable entity identifier used across the site.' },
  { file: 'people.json', name: 'AI people', page: '/people/',
    desc: 'People index: who is tracked, who has a full profile, and the identifier for each.' },
  { file: 'research.json', name: 'AI research library', page: '/research/',
    desc: 'Papers sorted into ten topics, with authors, venue, year, and citation counts.' },
  { file: 'mcp.json', name: 'MCP server registry', page: '/mcp/',
    desc: 'Model Context Protocol servers mirrored from the official registry.' },
  { file: 'weeks.json', name: 'This Week in AI', page: '/this-week-in-ai/',
    desc: 'The weekly digest index with permalinked ISO-week archives.' },
  { file: 'sources.json', name: 'Sources and references', page: '/sources/',
    desc: 'The primary-source bibliography that grounds every fact on the site.' },
];

// Only advertise what actually shipped in this build. An endpoint listed here
// but missing from public/api/ would be the same mistake that produced the
// 404 this page exists to fix.
const live = endpoints.filter((e) => existsSync(`public/api/${e.file}`));

const desc =
  `Public JSON endpoints for The World of AI: AI legislation, lawsuits, glossary, compliance ` +
  `frameworks, tools, companies, people, research, and MCP servers. Free to use with ` +
  `attribution, no key required, refreshed daily.`;

const jsonld = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebAPI',
  name: 'The World of AI public data API',
  description: desc,
  url: 'https://theworldofai.org/api/',
  documentation: 'https://theworldofai.org/api/',
  provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'SRJ Consulting & Services LLC' },
});
---
<Base title="Public Data API: AI Laws, Lawsuits, Tools, and Research" description={desc} current="/api/" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <h1>Public data API</h1>

  <div class="answer-box">
    <p class="answer-label">The short answer</p>
    <p>
      Every dataset behind this site is published as static JSON at
      <code>https://theworldofai.org/api/</code>. There are <b>{live.length}</b> endpoints, no key
      is required, and they refresh once daily on the same run that rebuilds the pages. Use them
      freely with attribution back to the relevant page.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Endpoints</h2>
  <table class="ep">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Endpoint</th><th scope="col">What it holds</th><th scope="col">Page</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {live.map((e) => (
        <tr>
          <td><a href={`/api/${e.file}`}><code>/api/{e.file}</code></a></td>
          <td>{e.desc}</td>
          <td><a href={e.page}>{e.name}</a></td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>How to use them</h2>
  <p>
    Every file is plain JSON served over HTTPS as a static asset, so a plain GET is all that is
    needed and CORS is open. There is no rate limit beyond ordinary CDN fair use, no
    authentication, and no versioning scheme: the shape of a file can gain fields but existing
    fields are not renamed or removed, on the same principle that keeps published URLs stable.
  </p>
  <pre class="code"><code>curl -s https://theworldofai.org/api/laws.json | jq '.states | length'</code></pre>
  <p>
    Each file carries a <code>generated</code> date, which is the date the data was verified
    rather than the date it was fetched. Where a daily refresh cannot reach a source, the last
    verified snapshot is kept rather than publishing an unverified number, so a stale
    <code>generated</code> date is a real signal and worth checking.
  </p>

  <h2>Attribution</h2>
  <p>
    Use of this data is welcome, including commercially, provided it is attributed. Link back to
    the relevant page rather than to the JSON file, so readers land on the sourced version.
  </p>
  <div class="cite-box">
    <p><b>Suggested attribution</b></p>
    <code>Data from The World of AI, https://theworldofai.org/. Retrieved {new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}.</code>
  </div>

  <p class="api-line">
    See also <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> for the machine-readable site summary and
    <a href="/sitemap-index.xml">sitemap-index.xml</a> for every URL.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .answer-box { background: #FFF6EC; border: 1px solid #F0D6B0; border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 22px 26px; margin: 18px 0 24px; max-width: 780px; }
  .answer-box p { font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.75; color: #2C2C2A; margin: 0; }
  .answer-label { font-size: 11px !important; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .16em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: #F07800; margin: 0 0 8px !important; }

  .ep { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: .6em 0 1.4em; font-size: .95rem; }
  .ep th, .ep td { text-align: left; padding: .55em .6em; border-bottom: 1px solid #ececf2;
    vertical-align: top; }
  .ep th { font-size: .82rem; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #6b6b78; }
  .ep code { font-size: .9rem; white-space: nowrap; }

  .code { background: #f7f7fb; border-left: 3px solid #201868; padding: .8em 1em;
    overflow-x: auto; font-size: .9rem; }
  .cite-box { margin-top: 1.2em; padding: .9em 1em; background: #f7f7fb;
    border-left: 3px solid #201868; font-size: .9rem; }
  .cite-box code { display: block; margin-top: .3em; word-break: break-word; }
  .api-line { margin-top: 1em; font-size: .87rem; color: #6b6b78; }
</style>
